{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>His eyes are darker than wine.</b> [This is] an adjective [form], called שנים on account of rows of teeth, because they are two rows. The Gaon [Saadia], of blessed memory, said: חכלילי עינים [his eyes are dark] — more than wine. Likewise he rendered מחלב [as] 'from milk.' Others say: 'לבן שינים' — that he will not eat anything impure nor stray after his eyes, and this is a distorted derash." "He mentioned the tribes at the beginning in the order they were born, except that he put Zebulun before Issachar because his inheritance fell between Zebulun and Dan:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון as the Gaon [Saadia] per standard convention; 'rendered' translates אמר in the sense of providing the Arabic translation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:27.479696859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}